### Sample requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8090

### Login as the bootstrap admin -> copy accessToken into @adminToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@tickets.local", "password": "Admin@12345"}

###
@adminToken = paste-admin-token-here

### Admin: create an event
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Rock Night",
  "description": "Live bands all night",
  "venue": "City Arena",
  "startsAt": "2030-06-01T19:00:00Z",
  "price": 25.00,
  "totalSeats": 100
}

### Admin: cancel an event
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/events/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Public: list events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/events

### Register a customer -> copy accessToken into @token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "alice@example.com", "password": "Password123", "fullName": "Alice"}

###
@token = paste-customer-token-here

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Book tickets (any client-side price is ignored)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId": 1, "quantity": 2}

### My bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel a booking
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bookings/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
